hako-launcher (0.4.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * hako-screen-idle: turns the panel backlight off when no input device
    (pads, buttons, touch, keyboards) has been used for a while, and back on
    at the next input, which is kept from the app. Settings: "Screen off"
    (never / 1 / 3 / 5 / 10 / 30 minutes, default 5).
  * Settings rows a little lower again for the new item.

 -- hako-os <hako@hako-os>  Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:30:00 +0900

hako-launcher (0.3.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Settings: Bluetooth screen. Switch the adapter on and off, search for
    devices, pair (+ trust) and connect a new device, connect / disconnect a
    paired one, and forget it (X). Talks to BlueZ over D-Bus (sd-bus) and
    registers a NoInputNoOutput agent for pairing game pads and headphones.
  * Settings rows are a little lower again to fit the new item.
  * Every connected gamepad drives the launcher (the built-in pad and, say, a
    Bluetooth one), not only the first one found.

 -- hako-os <hako@hako-os>  Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +0900

